        "AC 7 PASS: zero matches for project_slug, filterProject, and scope === 'project' in knowledge.js (grep verified).",
        "BLOCKER: styles.css missing badge-scope-repository rule — repo scope badge renders unstyled. Fix required before PASS."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "tests_passed": 6,
        "tests_failed": 1
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "bug",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-30T11:07:22Z",
          "note": "styles.css: .badge-scope-repository CSS rule is missing. knowledge.js line 117 assigns class 'badge badge-scope-repository' to non-global scope badges, but styles.css only defines .badge-scope-global and .badge-scope-project (the latter now orphaned). Repository scope badge renders with .badge base styles only — no background colour or text colour. Developer must: (1) rename/replace .badge-scope-project with .badge-scope-repository (suggested: green tones matching the old project rule: background:#dcfce7; color:#15803d); (2) rename/replace [data-theme=\"dark\"] .badge-scope-project with [data-theme=\"dark\"] .badge-scope-repository (suggested: background:#14532d; color:#86efac). File: mcp-server/gui/public/styles.css lines 2446–2449 and 2517–2520."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-30T11:07:22Z",
